    "topicId": "d1-identity-federation",
    "type": "multi",
    "stem": "A startup is building a serverless mobile application and has these requirements:\n- Manage user sign-up and sign-in with email and Google, and enforce MFA.\n- After login, let the app call Amazon S3 and Amazon DynamoDB directly using temporary, per-user, least-privilege AWS credentials.\nWhich TWO components should the architecture use together to satisfy BOTH requirements? (Choose TWO.)",
