    "topicId": "d2-ha-ft",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A serverless application uses AWS Lambda functions that open direct connections to an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. Under spiky load the database exhausts its max_connections, and during Multi-AZ failovers the application suffers long reconnection delays because it caches the previous writer's DNS. Which addition BEST solves BOTH problems with the LEAST application change?",
