    "domainId": "d2",
    "topicId": "d2-ha-ft",
    "type": "multi",
    "stem": "A three-tier application runs across two Availability Zones, but a resilience review flags two single points of failure: all outbound internet traffic from private instances flows through one NAT gateway located in AZ-A, and the database is a self-managed MySQL server on a single EC2 instance. Which TWO changes BEST improve fault tolerance? (Choose TWO.)",
