    "topicId": "d2-storage-resilience",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A data analytics team stores 20 TB of intermediate result files in S3. The files are read a few times each week, and if any file is lost it is automatically re-created from the source data lake during the next nightly pipeline run. The team wants the LOWEST-cost S3 storage while still accessing objects through the standard S3 API with millisecond retrieval. Which storage class is the MOST cost-effective choice?",
