    "inShort": "Multi-AZ keeps a synchronous standby in a second AZ and flips the DNS name to it automatically, so data loss is near zero and no one has to intervene.",
    "trap": "Read replicas in other AZs (B): they look like redundancy, but replication is asynchronous (possible data loss) and promotion is manual, so it is not automatic HA.",
    "confusableId": "cmp-multiaz-readreplica"
