    "topicId": "d3-networking-perf",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A financial-services company runs an on-premises data center that transfers roughly 5 TB of analytics data to Amazon S3 and RDS every night. The batch jobs are missing their window because throughput over the existing internet-based tunnel is inconsistent, and the security team requires traffic to avoid the public internet. Latency and bandwidth must be predictable month over month. Which connectivity option is the MOST appropriate?",
