    "topicId": "d3-networking-perf",
    "type": "multi",
    "stem": "A news website serves most of its pages and images through Amazon CloudFront with an S3 and ALB origin. Engineers notice the CloudFront cache hit ratio is low and the origin is under heavy load because many requests are being forwarded to it. They want to increase the proportion of requests served directly from the edge caches and offload the origin. Which TWO actions BEST improve the cache hit ratio? (Choose TWO.)",
