    "explanation": "AWS Client VPN is a managed, elastic OpenVPN-based endpoint that lets individual users connect from a software client on their device to resources in a VPC (and, with routing, to on-premises networks). It scales with the number of connections and supports certificate-based and directory/SAML authentication, matching a variable remote workforce.\n\nYou would not use AWS Site-to-Site VPN because it connects an entire on-premises network (a customer gateway device) to AWS, not individual roaming laptops. You would not use AWS Direct Connect because it is a dedicated physical circuit installed at a fixed location, which cannot serve mobile home users. AWS Storage Gateway is a hybrid storage service and is unrelated to remote user network access.\n\nFor the exam, also know the key distinction: Client VPN is client-to-site (individual users), while Site-to-Site VPN is network-to-network (whole sites). Both use IPsec/TLS over the internet, but they solve different connectivity problems.",
    "difficulty": 2,
