    "correct": [
      "A"
    ],
    "explanation": "AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) is the purpose-built service for lift-and-shift (rehost) server migrations. It installs a lightweight replication agent on each source server, continuously replicates the servers' block-level data into a staging area in AWS, and then launches production EC2 instances at cutover — minimizing downtime and requiring little to no application refactoring. It handles both physical and virtual (including VMware) Windows and Linux servers, making it the correct fit for migrating 250 mixed servers.\n\nYou would not use AWS Database Migration Service because DMS migrates databases, not entire bootable application servers. AWS Storage Gateway provides hybrid access to cloud-backed storage from on-premises applications; it is not a server migration tool. AWS DataSync moves files and objects between storage systems and cannot replicate and boot whole server workloads in EC2.\n\nFor the exam, map the 'migration' services to workloads: MGN rehosts servers (successor to CloudEndure Migration), DMS migrates databases, and DataSync transfers files/objects. When a question stresses lift-and-shift of servers with continuous replication and minimal cutover downtime, the answer is MGN.",
