    "topicId": "d4-storage-cost",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A SaaS company ingests user-uploaded datasets into Amazon S3. Some datasets are downloaded constantly for weeks and then go untouched for months; others are cold from day one but occasionally spike in popularity. Access patterns are unpredictable, and the team does not want to build or maintain lifecycle rules or pay retrieval fees. Which option MOST cost-effectively optimizes storage cost automatically?",
