    "explanation": "S3 Intelligent-Tiering automatically moves each object between frequent and infrequent access tiers (and optional archive tiers) based on observed usage, for a small per-object monitoring fee and with no retrieval charges. That makes it ideal for the unknown, shifting, and spiky access described here.\n\nYou would not use a Lifecycle rule to Standard-IA because lifecycle transitions assume predictable aging; here a cold object can suddenly spike, and a premature transition would incur IA retrieval fees exactly when the object gets popular. S3 One Zone-IA reduces durability to a single AZ and still does nothing to adapt to changing patterns. S3 Glacier Deep Archive is for long-term cold data with ~12-hour retrieval — unusable when an object might spike and need immediate access.\n\nFor the exam, also know the cost trade-off: Intelligent-Tiering charges a per-object monitoring/automation fee (objects under 128 KB are not monitored and are always billed at the frequent tier) but no retrieval fees, whereas Lifecycle is free to configure but leaves you paying IA/Glacier retrieval fees.",
