    "explanation": "AWS Cost Explorer visualizes historical spend (up to the past 12 months) and forecasts future cost, with filtering and grouping by service, linked account, or cost allocation tag — satisfying the visualization and forecasting need. AWS Budgets defines cost or usage thresholds and sends alerts (including when spend is forecast to exceed a limit) via email or Amazon SNS, satisfying the alerting need.\n\nYou would not rely on Amazon CloudWatch dashboards for this: CloudWatch tracks operational metrics and can surface an estimated-charges billing metric, but it does not provide Cost Explorer's cost breakdowns and forecasting. AWS Trusted Advisor flags cost-optimization opportunities such as idle resources, but it is not a spend-forecasting or budget-alerting tool. AWS Compute Optimizer recommends right-sizing for EC2, EBS, and Lambda based on performance, not cost dashboards or alerts.\n\nFor the exam, also know that when you need line-item granularity beyond Cost Explorer you use the AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR), and that cost allocation tags let you attribute spend to specific teams, projects, or environments.",
