    "topicId": "d4-compute-cost",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A retail company's e-commerce API runs on a fixed set of On-Demand EC2 instances. Traffic is very low overnight, ramps up each morning, and every weekday at exactly 12:00 there is a large, well-known lunchtime spike. Outside that window, the current fleet is heavily over-provisioned. The team wants to cut cost while ensuring capacity is ready before the predictable spike begins. What is the MOST cost-effective approach?",
