    "topicId": "d4-db-cost",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A SaaS company runs an internal analytics database on Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL. The application is used only during business hours and is completely idle nights and weekends, with traffic that ramps up and down unpredictably during the day. The team wants a relational engine that automatically matches capacity to demand and avoids paying for idle over-provisioned instances. Which option is the MOST cost-effective?",
