    "stem": "A company runs a steady, predictable production workload: an Amazon DynamoDB table with a well-understood constant throughput baseline, and an Amazon Aurora MySQL cluster that runs 24/7 all year. The finance team wants to lower database spend through commitments and capacity choices without changing the architecture. Which TWO actions will reduce cost for these steady workloads? (Choose TWO.)",
