    "explanation": "AWS Cost Explorer is purpose-built to visualize and analyze historical AWS spend, filter and group by service and cost-allocation tags, and forecast future cost. It lets the company break down database spend, spot trends, and pinpoint idle or over-provisioned resources to target for right-sizing, making it the correct tool.\n\nYou would not rely on CloudWatch metrics dashboards because they show operational/performance metrics (CPU, connections, IOPS) rather than dollar spend and forecasting; they help you decide sizing but do not analyze the bill. You would not use AWS Config because it tracks resource configuration and compliance history, not cost. You would not use CloudTrail because it records API activity for auditing and security, not billing analysis.\n\nFor the exam, also know the complementary tools: AWS Trusted Advisor flags specific idle or underutilized RDS instances and other cost-optimization checks, AWS Budgets alerts you when spend crosses thresholds, and Cost Explorer's rightsizing recommendations pair with CloudWatch utilization data to confirm a downsize is safe.",
