    "topicId": "d4-network-cost",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A three-tier application is deployed across three Availability Zones for high availability. The private subnets in all three AZs currently route outbound internet traffic through a single NAT gateway located in AZ-a. The architect notices unexpected cross-AZ data-transfer charges and is also concerned about resilience. What is the BEST way to address BOTH the cost and the availability issue?",
