    "inShort": "A NAT gateway in each AZ, used only by that AZ's own subnets, fixes the cross-AZ charges and the single point of failure at the same time.",
    "trap": "Two NAT gateways in AZ-a — 'redundancy' is tempting, but AZ-b and AZ-c still pay cross-AZ charges and an AZ-a outage still takes them all down."
