    "topicId": "d3-storage-perf",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "You are consolidating storage for a genomics company. A pipeline of Linux EC2 instances writes 30 TB of sequencing output over NFS, and a team of Windows analysts must then open those same files over SMB using their Active Directory credentials. Both protocols must see one copy of the data — duplicating the dataset into two file systems is unacceptable. Which AWS storage service BEST meets these requirements?",
