    "domainId": "d1",
    "topicId": "d1-network-security",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "You enabled IPv6 on a production VPC. Instances in a private subnet now have IPv6 addresses and must make outbound-only calls to an external IPv6 software-update API, but they must NOT be reachable from the internet. A NAT gateway already handles their IPv4 outbound traffic. What must you add so the IPv6 outbound path works while blocking inbound-initiated connections?",
