    "id": "d1-data-protection-44",
    "domainId": "d1",
    "topicId": "d1-data-protection",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "Your versioned Amazon S3 bucket has grown to 60 TB and storage cost is climbing because every overwrite keeps prior versions indefinitely. Policy says you must keep the current version and the previous versions for 30 days for recovery, then automatically delete previous versions older than that. What is the MOST cost-effective way to meet this?",
