    "topicId": "d2-ha-ft",
    "type": "multi",
    "stem": "You run a fleet of 60 Linux EC2 instances across three Availability Zones in an Auto Scaling group. Two requirements: (1) the CloudWatch agent and a hardened sshd configuration must always be present and be automatically reapplied whenever an instance drifts from that state, and (2) OS security patches must be installed automatically on a monthly schedule using an approved patch baseline. Which combination of AWS Systems Manager capabilities BEST meets both requirements? (Choose TWO.)",
