    "topicId": "d3-storage-perf",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "An existing SSD-backed Amazon FSx for Windows File Server share still has plenty of free space, but users report that file operations have become slow as the number of concurrent users has grown. You want to improve performance without recreating the file system and without paying for capacity you do not need. Which action MOST directly addresses the problem?",
