    "domainId": "d3",
    "topicId": "d3-storage-perf",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A climate-research team runs a nightly batch job on Amazon EC2 that reads a 12 TB dataset from beginning to end in long sequential passes, scanning the whole file to compute aggregates. The access pattern is almost entirely large sequential reads with very few random seeks, and the team wants the LOWEST-cost EBS volume that still delivers high streaming throughput. Which EBS volume type BEST fits?",
