    "stem": "A 100 GiB gp2 volume backs a small but write-heavy metadata database. It performs well when idle but collapses to about 300 IOPS under sustained load. You need a consistent 3,000 IOPS at the LOWEST cost, without over-provisioning capacity you do not need. What should you do?",
