    "id": "d3-compute-perf-55",
    "domainId": "d3",
    "topicId": "d3-compute-perf",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "Your compute tier scales elastically, but the Amazon Aurora MySQL cluster runs on a fixed db.r6g.2xlarge writer that sits nearly idle overnight and saturates during unpredictable daytime peaks. You want the database's compute capacity to scale up and down automatically in fine-grained steps without manually changing the instance class. Which approach BEST meets this need?",
