    "topicId": "d3-hybrid",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "You created an interface VPC endpoint for Amazon SQS so instances in a private subnet can reach SQS privately, and you enabled private DNS on the endpoint. Instances still resolve the default SQS service name to public IP addresses instead of the endpoint's private IPs. The VPC was built from a CloudFormation template with customized settings. What is the MOST likely cause?",
