    "topicId": "d3-networking-perf",
    "type": "single",
    "stem": "A voice-over-IP conferencing backend sits behind AWS Global Accelerator. Each caller's TCP signaling and UDP media packets must consistently reach the same backend endpoint for the duration of a call, but with the accelerator's default settings a caller's connections are sometimes routed to different endpoints mid-call. Which Global Accelerator setting enforces this stickiness?",
