    "explanation": "AWS Compute Optimizer analyzes CloudWatch utilization metrics and emits right-sizing recommendations for EBS volumes specifically — including gp2-to-gp3 migrations and reductions to over-provisioned IOPS and throughput on Provisioned IOPS volumes — each with an estimated monthly savings figure. It is free to enable and can be turned on across an organization, so it matches the multi-account requirement exactly.\n\nYou would not use Trusted Advisor here because its storage-related Cost Optimization checks find resources that are unused — unattached or underutilized EBS volumes, idle load balancers, unassociated Elastic IPs. It tells you what to delete, not which volume type or IOPS setting a busy volume should be changed to.\n\nYou would not use Cost Explorer because it reports what you were billed and forecasts trends. It can show that EBS spend is rising but has no view of volume utilization, so it cannot recommend gp2 to gp3.\n\nYou would not use S3 Storage Lens because it is an analytics tool for Amazon S3 object storage — bucket-level usage, activity, and storage-class distribution. It has no visibility into EBS at all.\n\nFor the exam, also know the division of labor: Compute Optimizer right-sizes what you are using, Trusted Advisor finds what you are not using, and Cost Explorer/CUR explain what you paid. Questions usually turn on which of those three verbs appears in the stem.",
    "difficulty": 2,
